        "mds:value": "Al2O3/AlN/InGaAs structures, AlN dielectric and oxide-semiconductor stacks.",
        "mds:quote": "Krylov et al. [... used oxygen-free AlN dielectric to reduce the interface state density..."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/InterfacialReactions": {
        "mds:value": "surface nitridation producing an essential increase in the NW conductivity... surface passivation.",
        "mds:quote": "[...] they found nitridation producing an essential increase in the NW conductivity and the µ-PL intensity as well as evidence of surface passivation. [...]"
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/InterfaceQualityControl": {
        "mds:value": "the insertion of the AlN layer significantly reduced the midgap interface states density, prevent indium out-diffusion phenomenon.",
        "mds:quote": "[...] frequency-dependent capacitance voltage measurements shown in Figure 12 demonstrated that the insertion of the AlN layer [...]"
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/MaterialStabilty": {
        "mds:value": "better thermochemical stability and higher band gap energy than ZnO",
        "mds:quote": "ZnS has better thermochemical stability and higher band gap energy than ZnO [36],"
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/MicroelectronicsDevices": {
        "mds:value": "Metal Interlayer Semiconductor (MIS) contacts, Non-alloyed S/D ohmic contact for III-V MOS.",
        "mds:quote": "[...] The source/drain contact resistance testing in Figure 10 showed that the current density of the SF6-treated MIS contact were about 4 times and 15 times larger than [...], proposed a promising non-alloyed S/D ohmic contact for III-V MOS."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/NativeOxidePassivation": {
        "mds:value": "Various techniques have been applied to improve the surface and interface quality, e.g., chemical etching, ion sputtering,",
